# Explainable Intervention Prioritization System (EIPS)
#
# What's deliberately left OUT of version control, and why:
#
# 1. Real MML data. The connected dataset is a genuine Limble CMMS export
#    (real asset registry + PM/work-order history from the mine site).
#    Even in a *private* GitHub repository, that data would sit in the
#    repo's history forever (every past commit, not just the latest
#    files) and would be visible to anyone ever given access to the repo
#    or invited as a Streamlit Cloud collaborator. The safer pattern is:
#    the code and the trained model ship in the repo, and the real data
#    is (re)loaded straight into the hosted database after deployment,
#    either through the app's own "Import Dataset" page or directly into
#    the hosted Postgres database -- never through git.
#
# 2. The local SQLite database file. It holds real predictions, machine
#    records, and -- once the login system is used -- account username/
#    password-hash rows. None of that belongs in source control, and once
#    the app is hosted it uses a separate Postgres database anyway (see
#    docs/deployment_guide.md), so this file is purely a local-dev
#    convenience.
#
# 3. Secrets. `.env` and `.streamlit/secrets.toml` hold the real
#    DATABASE_URL (with a password in it) once you have one. Only the
#    *.example templates are committed.

# --- Python ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# --- Virtual environments ---
venv/
.venv/
env/

# --- Secrets / environment ---
.env
.streamlit/secrets.toml

# --- Local database ---
database/*.db
database/*.sqlite
database/*.sqlite3

# --- Real / uploaded data (see note above) ---
data/raw/
data/interim/
data/processed/
data/uploads/
data/exports/

# --- Any bundled/backup data archive -- e.g. "Data Repo.zip", a full
#     backup of the original real dataset sitting at the project root.
#     Same reasoning as the data/ exclusions above: never belongs in git.
*.zip

# --- Logs ---
logs/*.log

# --- OS / editor noise ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/
